From 3e5258dbb3e168ea232a4bf734bc4ac5e9e94180 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 10:38:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rdnshc: the resolver health check takes an IPv6 server, gated
 on the router's IPv6 service

Owner review 2026-09-07 of the v3.1.1 health check: it was IPv4-only in five
places - the nvram field (CKN_STR15), cfg_read's AF_INET parse, the probe's
sockaddr_in/AF_INET socket, the INET_ADDRSTRLEN buffers, and the page
(maxlength 15, validator.ipv4_addr, the isIPAddr key filter). A LAN resolver
reached over IPv6, or an IPv6 WAN upstream, could not be watched.

- rc/rdnshc.c: the target is IPv4 or IPv6, kept in its canonical inet_ntop
  spelling (one form in the log); the probe builds a sockaddr_storage and opens
  a socket of the matching family; line_is_target() now compares the address
  in a server=/nameserver line BY VALUE (parsed, #port and %zone stripped), so
  "2001:DB8::1", "2001:db8:0:0::1" and "2001:db8::1#53" all match the one
  server - the textual compare could miss an IPv6 upstream the firmware wrote
  in another spelling. An IPv6 target while IPv6 is disabled on the router
  (ipv6_enabled()) makes the check idle: no route to it and no IPv6 upstream to
  move; one log line says so, the state reads off. Buffers sized INET6.
- shared/defaults.c: reaper_dnshc_target CKN_STR15 -> CKN_STR64 (the CKN_STR
  clamp would have cut an IPv6 spelling on apply).
- Advanced_System_Content.asp: maxlength 45, a key filter that admits digits,
  hex letters, dots and colons (rdhcKey), validation accepts IPv4 always and
  IPv6 only while ipv6_service is not "disabled" (isLegal_ipv6, muted, with
  the reason in the alert), and a note under the box; token RDHC_27 in all 25
  packs (lockstep 6895).

Gates: reaper_static_checks 11/11; mk-rc compiles and links clean, no
diagnostics in rdnshc.c. Verify marker added for the idle log line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
